He later rushed to the firing line of fire and leading the line forward before rackling only to a field shoot and knocked out three members of detachment.
Lieutenant-Colonel Vann was assassinated by a German sniper on October 4, 1918 just over a month before the end of the war.
Michael Vann, 72, said that his grandfather's actions were "something I'd know I can't match, but also something that makes me humble."
He and his brother Dr. James Vann laid a wreath after the parade led by the Brentwood Imperial Youth Band.
